  "title": "Variance",
  "slug": "variance",
  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:variance",
  "domain": "data",
  "definition": "The fundamental statistical measure of dispersion, defined as the expected squared deviation of a random variable from its mean, Var(X) = E[(X \u2212 E[X])\u00b2]. Its square root is the standard deviation; its multivariate generalisation is the covariance matrix; and it parameterises the spread of the Gaussian distribution. Variance governs the reliability of sample-based estimates, decomposes prediction error in the bias-variance trade-off, and is the quantity that variance-reduction techniques in Monte Carlo estimation and stochastic optimisation exist to control.",
